    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i guess... but the thing is, a \"small moment of peace\" feels like such a lie in the story. it feels dishonest to give him a little break when the reality of his situation is just... it's inevitable. like, if you're drowning, a tiny moment of breathing doesn't actually change the fact that you're going under. i feel like the story is begging for something more permanent. something that actually resolves the tension instead of just delaying it. does that even make sense for a character arc?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
